          The fitness industry has spent a decade convincing people that a home gym is a five-figure project. It is not. A complete barbell setup — rack, bar, three hundred pounds of plates, an adjustable bench, and rubber flooring over a protected slab — comes in under fifteen hundred dollars if you know which corners are safe to cut and which absolutely are not. We built exactly that gym, trained in it for a full year through a humid summer and a freezing winter, and this is what survived.
